[Music]  hi my name is Kate some ways I come from  Birmingham in England but I study in  Cardiff in Wales through the Erasmus  program I was able to spend some time  both in France and Italy as I study  French and Italian whilst in France I  worked at Disney Ursa which is Institute  and for my cheeks at avi Hall and there  I worked with disabled adults teaching  English for the second half of my year I  was in Venice Italy and there I studied  at the University named careful scurry  moving to France was a massive change  for me as it meant moving from the  capital city Cardiff to a small town it  was completely different for me to be  taught totally in one language I found  that even though I was learning facts in  that language I was also thinking about  the way they were being presented when I  was studying Italian in Cardiff I  remember thinking to myself this is  great but how could I really really  learn this language the best way to do  it is obviously go to the country then  you're speaking everyday and you're  picking up words without even knowing it  you're out for dinner with a friend and  you order a pizza and realize you just  learnt the word for mushroom or  something it's some very enriching  experience so do you think you would  ever go back definitely  I say when you get back it is quite  tough you get this kind of like Erasmus  blues because you just want to go back  again I would like to say thank you for  the opportunity to do Erasmus because it  means I've grown into a full rounded  individual and I know that when I  finished my studies I will maybe just  get that bit higher mark from doing  Erasmus and that will really help me out  in the job market in the future to  anyone who's thinking of doing a Rasmus  please just go and do it it's such a  great opportunity to go abroad meet  people improve your language learning  skills you'll be able to do everything  there so please just give it a go my  name is Marcela sublimino I live in shop  Anja Arden it's a beautiful region as  you can see 23 years old and then right  now standing in front of my school where  I run the industry of production and  management during this era CMAs program  in Romania I  in the company called hotel where I had  to accomplish a management project did  you improve your level in English yeah  because I had to speak English about  four three a month non-stop I had been  told before I go to Romania that it was  a very cold country I also had to to  find my technical words had been told  also that the people wasn't as friendly  as as they are actually and I noticed  that it was wrong it's not very easy to  speak English every day and to get used  to explain something you're feeling what  I learned in the company is that  whatever happens I have to keep on  trying and not to give up until  something is done it's a way to prove  your independence to prove that you can  make things by your own to prove that  you that you can be a self-made man  my name is Petra novikova I'm 22 and I  study media and history in Masaryk  University in Brno Czech Republic right  now I'm just finishing my internship  here at NATO headquarters in Brussels  with the Erasmus programme right now we  are in a meeting room number one  where normally the North Atlantic  Council takes place which is the highest  authority of the whole NATO it's a world  world itself I would say this whole  organization when you speak the  international English but you can meet  people from all around the world and you  can see the cultural differences you can  see people coming in in different  uniforms so what was the best during my  Erasmus day it's the culture you have in  here you're you flatmates your new  friends you make in here they let me do  things you know it was faster it's not  just that you do part of a work and you  don't really see the result but I was  lucky that during my stay in here there  was a six  years of NATO big celebration and  Strasbourg and Kel and I was part of the  team who organized a big conference for  students more than 300 and Strasbourg  you know discussing NATO's future so  that's something like really you know a  result you can see on the spot actually  I just got a job here in Brussels and  I'm considering to stay because I  already have my new friends and my new  life in here although I'm still working  on a bachelor thesis for my university  there was Moses actually the thing which  inspired me my name is Peter Murphy on  22 years old and I study industrial  design at the National College of Art  Design in Dublin Ireland  and thanks to my Erasmus stay in Finland  for five months not only did I study  industrial design but I partook in a lot  of other modules also including  architecture Finnish cuisine learning  the Finnish language furniture design  product design and life drawing when I  was there I loved it it was fantastic we  had an introduction week into our  college they had a lot of events planned  for us which was brilliant we went snow  hiking we went snow skiing  the Erasmus luck for me is somewhat up  by saying it's an adventure  it's about leaving everything you're  comfortable with and dropping yourself  into a different environment making new  friends learning new language living on  your own for the first time the host  institution that I stayed in Lahti it  was impeccable really really good  college very well funded by the  government which was nice to see they  had a lot of materials and other  workshops on offer I like I learned a  lot of new trades the tutors of my host  institution had a real hands-on approach  to design there was a great emphasis on  the final product for example I was  doing a product on designing chairs and  in Dublin we might have maybe a 3d  picture of the chair or very renard  sketches but in Finland I was actually  made to make the chair out of wood so  there was a whole learning process not  only was i sketching I was making the  piece out of wood and at the end of the  day I had a quite fantastic looking  finished product when I came back to  Dublin I was faced with normal life  again I had parents to deal with  I had a loan to pay off  job so it was sort of like the Erasmus  blues  [Music]

